course: dictionary
lesson: 6045
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word memory has three main meanings, and the sentence around it tells you which one to use. Memory can be the ability of your brain to keep and remember things. It can also be a single thing you remember from the past, or the part of a computer where information is stored.
explain: «Memory games, like looking at objects on a tray and then naming them, train your attention.» Here memory is about the brain's ability, and games help it get stronger. In «people who were worried about us can look, in our memory, as if they were laughing», memory is a picture kept from the past.
explain: Ask yourself which meaning fits. Try swapping in «the brain's ability to remember» or «a remembered moment» and see which one makes sense. Phrases like «from memory» (without looking) and «in memory of» (to honour someone who has died) have their own meanings too, so read the whole phrase, not just the one word.
fact: Memory is the ability of your brain to keep and remember things.
fact: A memory is something you remember from the past.
fact: A computer's memory is the part where it stores information.
fact: «From memory» means without looking, so you know it well enough to say it from your own brain.
fact: Computer memory is measured in bytes, megabytes and gigabytes.
fact: Sleep helps memory, so a good night's sleep helps you learn your spellings and times tables.
exercise: «Grey squirrels bury nuts in many separate spots and find many by memory and smell.» What does finding them by memory mean? | *Using what they remember of where they hid them | By chance, with no thinking at all | By following other squirrels | By digging up the whole garden
exercise: «Memory games, like looking at objects on a tray and then naming them, train your attention.» What do memory games train? | Your handwriting | Your legs | *Your attention | Your singing voice
exercise: Families plant a tree «in memory of» Grandad. What does «in memory of» mean? | To hide something from people | *To honour someone who has died | To remember where the tree was bought | To copy the way Grandad planted trees
test: Mia can say her times tables «from memory». What does «from memory» mean? | Loudly and clearly | *Without looking | With a notebook open | Only on a Tuesday
test: The computer has 8 gigabytes of memory. Memory is measured in what? | *Bytes | Metres | Litres | Grams
exam: Which meaning of memory fits best in «Ravi has a good memory for names»? | A loud noise | The part of a computer that stores information | A kind of cake | *The brain's ability to keep and remember things
